; Static half of the DNS sidecar's zone (test/compose.yaml's `dns`
; service, test/dns/Corefile). IPs match the fixed addresses compose
; assigns mail-a/mail-b. The dynamic half - DKIM TXT records, which only
; exist once a server has generated its per-domain key at first start - is
; $INCLUDE'd from generated/dkim.zone, written by the dns_sidecar fixture
; in conftest.py. See test/README.md "DNS sidecar".
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 300
@   IN SOA ns.example. admin.example. ( 1 3600 600 86400 300 )
@   IN NS ns.example.
ns  IN A 172.30.0.53

a                   IN A   172.30.0.10
mail-a.a            IN A   172.30.0.10
a                   IN MX  10 mail-a.a.example.

b                   IN A   172.30.0.11
mail-b.b            IN A   172.30.0.11
b                   IN MX  10 mail-b.b.example.

$INCLUDE /etc/coredns/generated/dkim.zone
